WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:11.467
This is the chapter's lab: choose an example, the target K and the capacity C, and change any node's size.

2
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:16.267
G01 at capacity 2: step one merges A–B, size 2, legal.

3
00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:24.067
Step two: the highest-affinity AB–C has size 3, over capacity, marked red and skipped; D–E instead.

4
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:31.533
Jump to the end: it stops at AB | C | DE. The report is separate: legal, but K is not reached.

5
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:40.667
The diagnosis: the bound ⌈5/2⌉ = 3 already exceeds K, so the target is impossible and greedy stopping is not a mistake.

6
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:50.933
Switch to the original author's greedy_trap: greedy stops at 3 clusters, yet search finds the legal AC | BD. Diagnosis: greedy is stuck.

7
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:58.200
suboptimal: greedy cut 18, the exhaustive optimum 11. Legal and K reached, but not optimal.

8
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:08.136
Back to G01 at capacity 3, with A's size set to 2: the result changes from ABC | DE to AB | CDE, cut 5.

9
00:01:08.136 --> 00:01:18.269
The code lab: your code runs in the browser, with no Python to install. The greedy loop and the exhaustive oracle are already written.

10
00:01:18.269 --> 00:01:24.736
Run the checks first: neither task is written yet, so the result is INCOMPLETE.

11
00:01:24.736 --> 00:01:36.308
Task 1: report four separate items. Legal checks every cluster's size, K reached checks the count, and the main loop gives the stop reason.

12
00:01:36.308 --> 00:01:55.342
Task 2: classify. If K is not reached, check the bound, then the search; if it is, compare the cuts.

13
00:01:55.342 --> 00:02:02.742
Run the checks: everything passes, including an over-capacity node and a graph with no edges.

14
00:02:02.742 --> 00:02:11.275
Below, your functions run on eight cases, including a new graph, compared item by item with the course engine.

15
00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:19.142
All five diagnoses appear, and all agree. Click the greedy_trap row to draw your result on the left.

16
00:02:19.142 --> 00:02:26.275
Finally, try the challenges to check you really understand. Results stay in your browser.
